    <briefdescription>
<para>Decoder for the <ref refid="namespacetle92466ed_1_1FB__IMIN__IMAX" kindref="compound">FB_IMIN_IMAX</ref> register (<ref refid="namespacetle92466ed_1_1ChannelReg_1a268314fe1df66390c9a20a79630a1b8e" kindref="member">ChannelReg::FB_IMIN_IMAX</ref>). </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Per datasheet \u00a75.3.3.17 p.101, <ref refid="namespacetle92466ed_1_1FB__IMIN__IMAX" kindref="compound">FB_IMIN_IMAX</ref> is a 22-bit reply frame containing two 10-bit SIGNED (two&apos;s-complement) fields:</para>
<para>bits 9:0 IMIN I_min = &lt;IMIN&gt; \u00b7 4 A / (2^9 \u2212 1) = &lt;IMIN&gt; \u00b7 4 A / 511 bits 19:10 IMAX I_max = &lt;IMAX&gt; \u00b7 4 A / 511 bits 21:20 reserved</para>
<para>Full-scale range is approximately \u00b14 A (values 512\u2026\u22121 map to \u22124.007\u2026+4.0 A). Negative values represent recirculation current.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>The previous driver decoded these as unsigned 8-bit halves; that rendered all min/max reports garbage. Always route through this namespace. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
